    "body": "## Summary\n- stop relying on `pending[0]` to decide which recoverable publication receives Stripe initialization\n- re-read the authenticated pending-publication list before preparing payment\n- require an explicit publication choice when multiple recoverable attempts exist\n- bind PaymentIntent creation, polling, cancellation and Stripe return URL to the selected publication id\n- refresh remaining recoverable attempts after cancellation\n- document the multi-publication recovery invariant\n\n## Financial / privacy safety\n- selection is UI-only and does not mutate wallet reservations or ledger entries\n- no new publication or PaymentIntent is created until one existing attempt is unambiguous\n- pending-publication discovery remains owner-scoped via the existing backend endpoint\n- no job payload or private location data is exposed in the chooser\n\n## Validation\nCI should run the existing production dependency audit, frontend lint/build, Maven/API verify and runtime/payment smoke suites on the exact PR head.",
